-- B_k for k from 0, n of them: cs are the coordinates of M^k E b_g in the attached vertex's kernel basis (its
-- monomials ms2, basis bs2), tm is M there; each is lifted, mapped back by R, and read at the vertex's free
-- coordinates frsW (monomials msW). The spaces' data are arguments, computed once by the caller.
b-mats : Nat → List Nat → Mons → Mons → Rows → Rows → (List Nat → List Nat → SQ) → Rows → List Rows
b-mats n frsW msW ms2 bs2 tm rent cs = case n of
  zero → nil
  suc g → cons (restrict frsW (rows-map-entry rent msW ms2 (lift-all (mons-count ms2) bs2 cs))) (b-mats g frsW msW ms2 bs2 tm rent (rows-apply-all tm cs))
